invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_mont.c
catches: rsa_avx2_model_test
reason: rsa_mont.c's use_avx2 answers 0 whatever the session's ch_cfg.cpu
  says, so no session runs the AVX2 RSA kernel and CH_CPU_AVX2 picks
  nothing for RSA. Every byte stays right, because rsa_mont64.c computes
  the same bytes; only the time is wrong. bin/rsa_avx2_model_test counts
  the calls rsa_vp1_cpu makes into rsa_avx2_public over the lane model
  and requires one under the bit for every modulus the kernel takes.

--- old
    return (cpu & CH_CPU_AVX2) != 0;
--- new
    (void)cpu;
    return 0;
